I found a release-blocking contract gap despite the green happy-path gates. The implementation can report a native control as applied before its real installation point, and a control-application failure can occur only after the worker has already started—contrary to the accepted single pre-worker failure boundary. There is also an unhandled child-start failure that dereferences a nil `ProcessState`. I’m recording this as changes requested with exact rework tests, then routing the task to `to-dev`.
